><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251112145732+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="23702b43-d815-403d-9aa8-55ec142976d3" date="D:20251112145737+10'00'" name="55e2799d-b263-43a9-a02a-84c784c782d1" icon="Comment" page="7" rect="66.984756,172.388062,90.984756,196.388062" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Elite youth male and female basketball players with PT&#xD;adopted a landing strategy that decreased their loading rate&#xD;via a longer stance phase duration to achieve similar peak&#xD;forces during a stop-jump landing task as opposed to the&#xD;control participants. It remains unknown if this decrease in&#xD;loading rate in these PT players was a strategy to reduce&#xD;pain on landing. Athletes with PT reported reduced training&#xD;volume but not game time; however, it remains unknown&#xD;if this was an injury management strategy and/or if this </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>reduction in training affected their athlete development.&#xD;Future studies could adopt a longitudinal study design in&#xD;order to provide further insight into the cause and effect&#xD;mechanisms of this injury.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="7" rect="595.276001,104.388062,779.276001,196.388062"
/></text
